    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneI_10.3/p@37022",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "HASTINGS.\nGrant that our hopes, yet likely of fair birth,\nShould be still-born, and that we now possess’d\nThe utmost man of expectation,\nI think we are a body strong enough,\nEven as we are, to equal with the King.",
